# Procedural Glyph Library (Sanitized Backup)

This backup summarizes the procedural glyph workflow while withholding proprietary tooling and datasets.

## Glyph Path Generation
- Glyph outlines are reconstructed from the internal font repository and normalized to a unit coordinate space before rasterization.
- Runtime registration permits scenes to provide custom outlines that override the default catalog.
- Curve tessellation thresholds, font ingestion routines, and other sensitive logic are [REDACTED].

## SDF Integration
- Glyph paths feed the shared SDF generator so text renders consistently alongside other procedural sprites.
- Texture caching keys, smoothing heuristics, and GPU resource contracts are [REDACTED].

## External Sources
- Third-party font inputs must satisfy licensing checks and dimensional validation.
- Vendor-specific normalization data, licensing audits, and import transforms are [REDACTED].
